i89|v|To determine judicially by authority, or by decree; to constitute by edict; to appoint by decree or law; to determine; to order; to ordain; as, a court decrees a restoration of property. ; To ordain by fate. ; To make decrees; -- used absolutely.	s:tad,106,6~tad,106,6
ia9|v|To set apart and consecrate, as to a divinity, or for sacred uses; to devote formally and solemnly; as, to dedicate vessels, treasures, a temple, or a church, to a religious use. ; To devote, set apart, or give up, as one's self, to a duty or service. ; To inscribe or address, as to a patron.	o:22cu,24,5~22cu,24,5
