icz|n|Want or absence of something necessary for completeness or perfection; deficiency; -- opposed to superfluity. ; Failing; fault; imperfection, whether physical or moral; blemish; as, a defect in the ear or eye; a defect in timber or iron; a defect of memory or judgment.	a:1era,19,3~1era,19,3	v:1800,90,3~1800,90,3	V:bah,83,3;a7s,65,5~a7s,65,5;bah,83,3	n:1800,74,1~1800,74,1
