im2|a|Weighing facts and arguments with a view to a choice or decision; carefully considering the probable consequences of a step; circumspect; slow in determining; -- applied to persons; as, a deliberate judge or counselor. ; Formed with deliberation; well-advised; carefully considered; not sudden or rash; as, a deliberate opinion; a deliberate measure or result. ; Not hasty or sudden; slow.	j:ug1,56,3;wj,52,4;n5s,50,4;19wn,48,2;cdy,48,4;5cw,45,1;1krd,44,4;1j90,42,3;2881,14,3~wj,52,4;1krd,44,4;n5s,50,4;cdy,48,4;ug1,56,3;1j90,42,3;2881,14,3;19wn,48,2;5cw,45,1
